    {
      "id": "c48-business_rule",
      "kind": "business_rule",
      "text": "- LLM work must never run client-side.\n- Coach-facing insight reads must scope through assigned teams, not broad player access.\n- Player-facing feedback must be tied to the authenticated player and revalidate the affected dashboard surfaces.\n- Coach-to-team ownership is via `golf_team_coach_staff`; do not infer it from `golf_coaches.team_id`.\n- V2/V3 scoring and generator logic should stay pure where designed as pure engine code; Supabase access belongs in loaders, actions, or orchestration boundaries.\n- Citations, evidence, and baseline comparisons are part of the trust contract. Do not emit fabricated comparisons or uncited claims.\n- Budget-sensitive LLM behavior should use team settings and persisted usage, not hardcoded token math.",
      "source": {
        "kind": "feature_doc",
        "path": "memory/features/coachhelm-ai.md",
        "line": 73,
        "heading": "Business Rules"
      },
      "date": null,
      "sha": null,
      "refs": {
        "paths": [],
        "globs": [],
        "identifiers": [
          "golf_team_coach_staff",
          "golf_coaches"
        ]
      },
      "verified": "not_checked"
    },
    {
      "id": "c49-ui_contract",
      "kind": "ui_contract",
      "text": "- Coach views need fast triage: new, acknowledged, dismissed, resolved, and priority states must be visible.\n- Player views need clear actionability: what changed, why it matters, and what to do next.\n- Loading states should use skeletons that match final layout.\n- Empty states should stay compact and explain whether there is no data, no permission, or no insight yet. The Ask page's `ProgramOpening` renders a compact honest empty state when the program pulse has no items (2026-08-26) — it must never return nothing and leave the column blank.\n- Mobile views must use the shared app shell, Standard or Action headers, and bottom-nav clearance from `AGENTS.md`.\n- The Ask composer autofocuses only on fine-pointer (desktop) clients (2026-08-26). On touch, no CoachHelm surface may focus a text input on open — iOS answers that focus with a keyboard over an unread page.\n- The phone Ask drawer (`CoachHelmDrawer`) lifts by `--keyboard-height` and the composer drops its home-indicator pad while `body.keyboard-open` (2026-09-02) — the WebView never resizes for the keyboard, so a `bottom-0` drawer put the composer under the keys exactly like the messages screen.\n- A question started on the Brief tab (`CoachIntelligenceHome` → `?q=` → the Ask page) auto-submits exactly once through `PromptComposer`'s own `submit()` (2026-09-02) — it previously only pre-filled the composer, so the coach had to press Send a second time on the page it navigated to. `AskSurface` strips `q` from the URL the moment the submit is kicked off, before the server has minted a conversation, so a refresh or back-navigation in that window cannot resend it. `PromptComposer` also now restores the just-submitted text into the field on a failed turn (never on success) instead of the previous unconditional clear-on-submit, so a failure does not force retyping. See `src/components/golf/coachhelm/chat/PromptComposer.tsx`, `CoachHelmChat.tsx` (`autoSubmitInitialInput`), and `AskSurface.tsx`.",
      "source": {
        "kind": "feature_doc",
        "path": "memory/features/coachhelm-ai.md",
        "line": 83,
        "heading": "UI Contract"
      },
      "date": null,
      "sha": null,
      "refs": {
        "paths": [
          "src/components/golf/coachhelm/chat/PromptComposer.tsx"
        ],
        "globs": [],
        "identifiers": []
      },
      "verified": "not_checked"
    },
    {
      "id": "c50-risk",
      "kind": "risk",
      "text": "- Generated insight evidence can drift from real data if adapters or fallback paths skip citation validation.\n- Safety-net fallback behavior can mask generator failures if logs are ignored.\n- Course-management \"worst holes\" and hole-1 \"warmup\" insights require at\n  least five samples, matching the persisted insight writer's Rule 1\n  validation contract (`upsertInsight` throws `InsightEvidenceRefusal` below\n  the floor). `generateWorstHolesInsights` and `generateWarmupHoleInsight`\n  (`src/lib/coachhelm/v2/mining/course-management.ts`) route that refusal\n  through `isEvidenceRefusal()` and log it as a quiet, non-paging event —\n  the same pattern `v3/composite/synthesis.ts` uses. Before this was wired\n  up, the refusal reached `logServerError` unconditionally and paged as a\n  production incident (fingerprint `ea766422`, \"worst_holes upsert failed\").\n- A completed round's CoachHelm terminal state is written only through the\n  service-only `record_round_coachhelm_terminal_state` RPC. It may update\n  processing metadata but cannot modify score, shots, identity, or status.\n- Round-review feedback and player acknowledgement paths can become stale if revalidation misses player or coach routes.\n- V3 feature surface is expanding quickly; registry/docs must be updated when new generators, tables, or cron routes land.",
      "source": {
        "kind": "feature_doc",
        "path": "memory/features/coachhelm-ai.md",
        "line": 94,
        "heading": "Known Risk Areas"
      },
      "date": null,
      "sha": null,
      "refs": {
